    "https://www.csustan.edu/hr/career-opportunities/applicant-faqs": {
      "title": "Primary navigation",
      "description": "Applicant FAQs | California State University Stanislaus Skip to main content Menu Close Primary navigation myStanState Give Apply Search Menu Close Main navigation menu Main navigation Admissions & Aid Explore Admissions & Aid Overview Undergraduate Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Overview Apply to Stan State Freshman Admission Transfer Admission Returning Admission Dates & Deadlines Contact Admissions Office Graduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Overview Explore the Programs How to Apply I Have Applied Current Graduate Students Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid & Scholarships Overview Financial Aid Basics FA Online Forms Portal & Documents Scholarships Financial Wellness Satisfactory Academic Progress Contact Financial Aid Office Tuition & Fees Tuition & Fees Overview Fee Schedules & Deadlines Cashiers & Payment Information Direct Deposit Information General FAQs Majors & Programs Campus Life About Explore About Overview Accreditation & Achievements Our History Mission, Vision & Values Points of Pride University Leadership Contact Information Give Now Quick Links Incoming Students Academic Calendar Academic Catalog People Search Athletics News Events Utility Students Faculty Staff Alumni / Stockton Campus Library / A-Z Maps / Applicant FAQs Breadcrumb Home Human Resources Career Opportunities Applicant FAQs All Human Resources Section Menu close Human Resources Career Opportunities Applicant FAQs CSU Nondiscrimination Policy & Equal Employment Opportunity Professional Development Staff Recognition Telecommute Program Employee Benefits Payroll Hiring & Employment Resources Student Employee Resources Manager Resources CHRS ADA Accommodations Policies & Procedures Verification of Employment Self Service Separation From Employment Employee & Labor Relations Classification & Compensation Contact Information Contact Information (209) 667-3351 HR_Assistant@csustan.edu Mary Stuart Rogers, MSR 320 Division of Business & Finance Applicant FAQs Find answers to frequently asked questions. Expand all How do I set up an account to apply for jobs at Stan State? The University utilizes CHRS Recruiting, our online recruiting system, powered by PageUp. All applicants will need to create an account to apply for positions. To set up an account, click Apply Now on the position you are interested in. You will be prompted to enter a valid email address to create an account. On the “Personal Details” section of the application, you will create a password for your account that you will continue to use each time you log in. Please use the same email address each time you apply for a position. This will assist the University in processing your application as quickly as possible. Note: Please make sure your email address is current. How do I update my contact information (e.g. phone number or address change) in my Applicant Profile? Click on the Applicant Login button at Stan State Careers and log in with the email address and password associated with your account.  Click on “Update profile,” make your changes, and click Save. If the position you applied for is still posted, you can also update your application. I can’t remember my password. How do I reset it? Locate the Applicant Login button at Stan State Careers and click. You will see the login box with Email address and password. To reset your password, click “ Forgotten your password? ” link. Enter the email address associated with your account and click OK. An email will be sent that includes instructions on how to reset your password. How does the hiring process work? If you possess the minimum qualification for the position, as indicated by your application, your information will be reviewed by the hiring authority or search committee, as applicable. Upon the hiring authority or committee’s review of your qualifications, you may be contacted for an interview. If you successfully complete the interview process, the hiring department will check references, conduct a background check, and perform post-offer testing as required. I made a mistake on my application. How do I correct it? Prior to the deadline of the job posting, you can choose to withdraw your application by clicking the Withdraw button and resubmitting an application for that particular job posting. In the event you need to make corrections after the deadline, please contact us by phone for staff and management jobs at (209) 667-3351 or for faculty jobs at (209) 667-3392. Our hours of operation are 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. PST, Monday through Friday. Can I withdraw my application once I have submitted it for a specific job posting? Yes, you may withdraw your application. Log in to your account and click the button labeled Withdraw . If you would like to resubmit your application, you must do so prior to the deadline for the job posting. If you do not locate the Withdraw button, please contact us by phone for staff and management jobs at (209) 667-3351 or for faculty jobs at (209) 667-3392. Our hours of operation are 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. PST, Monday through Friday. Do I need to fill out all the fields in the application process? You are required to complete all information in the application process that has an asterisk (*) identifying the field as a required field. You will not be able to proceed in the application process if you do not complete the required fields. Who do I contact if I need an accommodation? Individuals may request a reasonable accommodation during the application and/or interview process. Please contact the Americans with Disabilities (ADA) Coordinator for assistance at (209) 667-3376. Updated: May 30, 2025 Search Footer Short Nav A-Z Directory People Search Main navigation Admissions & Aid Majors & Programs Campus Life About Give Now Footer menu Accessibility Annual Security Report Career Opportunities Contact Us Emergency Information Equity Programs/Title IX Maps & Directions Parenting Students Proud member of the California State University system © California State University, Stanislaus , One University Circle, Turlock, CA 95382 Website Copyright/DMCA Policy Modal Title ×"
    },
    "https://www.csustan.edu/hr/career-opportunities": {
      "title": "Primary navigation",
      "description": "Career Opportunities | California State University Stanislaus Skip to main content Menu Close Primary navigation myStanState Give Apply Search Menu Close Main navigation menu Main navigation Admissions & Aid Explore Admissions & Aid Overview Undergraduate Admissions Undergraduate Admissions Overview Apply to Stan State Freshman Admission Transfer Admission Returning Admission Dates & Deadlines Contact Admissions Office Graduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Overview Explore the Programs How to Apply I Have Applied Current Graduate Students Financial Aid & Scholarships Financial Aid & Scholarships Overview Financial Aid Basics FA Online Forms Portal & Documents Scholarships Financial Wellness Satisfactory Academic Progress Contact Financial Aid Office Tuition & Fees Tuition & Fees Overview Fee Schedules & Deadlines Cashiers & Payment Information Direct Deposit Information General FAQs Majors & Programs Campus Life About Explore About Overview Accreditation & Achievements Our History Mission, Vision & Values Points of Pride University Leadership Contact Information Give Now Quick Links Incoming Students Academic Calendar Academic Catalog People Search Athletics News Events Utility Students Faculty Staff Alumni / Stockton Campus Library / A-Z Maps / Career Opportunities Breadcrumb Home Human Resources Career Opportunities All Human Resources Section Menu close Human Resources Career Opportunities Applicant FAQs CSU Nondiscrimination Policy & Equal Employment Opportunity Professional Development Staff Recognition Telecommute Program Employee Benefits Payroll Hiring & Employment Resources Student Employee Resources Manager Resources CHRS ADA Accommodations Policies & Procedures Verification of Employment Self Service Separation From Employment Employee & Labor Relations Classification & Compensation Contact Information Contact Information (209) 667-3351 HR_Assistant@csustan.edu Mary Stuart Rogers, MSR 320 Division of Business & Finance Search Career Opportunities * Includes Coaches, Counselors & Librarians About Stan State California State University, Stanislaus serves a diverse student body of more than 10,000 at two locations in the Central Valley — a beautiful 228-acre campus in Turlock and the Stockton Campus . Widely recognized for its dedicated faculty and high-quality academic programs, the University offers a range of undergraduate and graduate programs and a doctorate in educational leadership. The University is a proud member of the 23-campus California State University system — the largest, the most diverse, and one of the most affordable university systems in the country. CSU campuses emphasize access to quality public higher education and workforce preparation responsive to regional needs. Our community is more than a collection of bright minds—CSU has attracted people with ambition, dedication and passion. The CSU Employee Profile tells the story of CSU’s workforce – arraying demographic data and celebrating outstanding achievements from throughout the system. Address: Stanislaus State One University Circle Turlock, California 95381 Maps & Parking Directions Human Resources (209) 667-3351 Faculty Affairs (209) 667-3392 Learn more About Stan State The CSU is a state entity whose business operations reside within the state of California. The CSU prohibits hiring employees to perform CSU-related work outside California. View the Out-of-State Employment Policy . Become a Warrior Campus Safety Pursuant to the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act , the Annual Security Report (ASR), is available viewing online. The ASR contains the current security and safety-related policy statements, emergency preparedness and evacuation information, crime prevention and sexual assault prevention information, and drug and alcohol prevention programming. The ASR also contains statistics of the Clery Act crimes for Stanislaus State for the previous three years. A paper copy of the ASR is available upon request by contacting the Office of the Clery Director located at One University Circle, Turlock, CA 95382, or by calling 209-667-3572. Updated: June 01, 2026 Search Footer Short Nav A-Z Directory People Search Main navigation Admissions & Aid Majors & Programs Campus Life About Give Now Footer menu Accessibility Annual Security Report Career Opportunities Contact Us Emergency Information Equity Programs/Title IX Maps & Directions Parenting Students Proud member of the California State University system © California State University, Stanislaus , One University Circle, Turlock, CA 95382 Website Copyright/DMCA Policy Modal Title ×"
